outputs.exact_statement:
For every dyadic cell $Q\subset R$ and every vector $a=(a_v)_{v\in\mathcal V(Q)}$, one has $$D^{-1}\|a\|_{\ell^2}
 \le \left\|\sum_{v\in\mathcal V(Q)}a_v\Phi_v(y)\right\|_{\mathcal H}
 \le D^{3/2}\|a\|_{\ell^2}
 \quad\hbox{for almost every }y\in Q.
 \label{eq:row-catalog-comparison}$$ In particular constant coefficients in such a representation are unique. Coefficients may be regarded as vectors in the one space $\ell^2(\mathcal V)$ by extending them by zero; the vector for a combination on $Q$ is unchanged when the combination is restricted to a descendant.*

*These assertions and the same value of $D$ hold after restriction to a dyadic subroot $R'\subset R$: discard birth cells disjoint from $R'$, give an inherited label with $R'\subset J_v$ the new birth cell $R'$, and retain the other birth cells contained in $R'$.

Let the root, catalog, partitions, and rows satisfy every hypothesis of Lemma <a href="#lem:row-maximal" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:row-maximal">17</a>. Let $(F_s)_{s\in\mathsf S}$ satisfy Equation <a href="#eq:row-input-normalization" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:row-input-normalization">[eq:row-input-normalization]</a> on $R$. Choose $s_n\in\mathsf S$ with $s_1\le s_2\le\cdots\le s_N$, and let every row of round $n$ read the same input $F_{s_n}$. These read indices label the input schedule independently of the spatial depths of the support cells. Then $$\left(\sum_{n=1}^N\sum_{\nu\in\mathcal R_n}
          \|A_\nu F_{s_n}\|_{\mathcal Y_\nu}^2\right)^{1/2}
 \le \mathfrak C_D B\,|R|^{1/2}
 \le \frac{40}{3} B\log_2(2D)\,|R|^{1/2}.
 \label{eq:row-depth}$$ The constant is independent of the number of rows, depths, and input blocks.

For the full endpoint outputs $Z_{G,s}=\overline L_{G,s}\mathcal B_sB_s$ just defined, let $\mathcal J$ be a common finite collection of depth intervals $[r,t]$ with edge-overlap multiplicity at most $a$. For each $G,[r,t]$, let $E_{G,r,t}$ be a union of $t$-cells having a downstream actual-use certificate for $G$. Then $$\sum_{G,[r,t]\in\mathcal J}
   \|\mathbf1_{E_{G,r,t}}(Z_{G,t}-Z_{G,r})\|_2^2
       \le aG_0|R|.
 \label{eq:h-certified-variation}$$ For one shared output $Z_s^{\rm sh}$ in the stated source class, let $E_{r,t}$ be the union of the required $t$-cells across all its uses. Then $$\sum_{[r,t]\in\mathcal J}
   \|\mathbf1_{E_{r,t}}(Z_t^{\rm sh}-Z_r^{\rm sh})\|_2^2
       \le aG_0|R|.$$ This shared assertion has no group sum or group certificate. All outputs before the attempt root are zero.
